// input: emitted
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not=idr.version --implicit-check-not=idr.entry --implicit-check-not=func.func{{.}}@ --implicit-check-not=idr.erased
// The contract the Idris side emits.
// The module carries idr.program, and no version, entry or entry kind.
// CHECK: module attributes {{[{][^}]*}}idr.program
// A data type declares its constructors, with the tags Idris gives them
// and their fields. An Idris name is a NameLoc around the source location.
// CHECK: idr.data @Prog.Shape{{.*}} {{[{]$}}
// CHECK-DAG: idr.ctor @Circle (i64) {{.*}}loc("Prog.Circle"("Prog.idr":
// CHECK-DAG: idr.ctor @Rect (i64, i64) {{.*}}loc("Prog.Rect"("Prog.idr":
// CHECK: } loc("Prog.Shape"("Prog.idr":
// Prog's value is a private function of no arguments. An erased argument
// is not passed: keep's witness is no argument of the call, and a call
// carries its source location. Under an idr.func, the dialect's ops print
// without their `idr.` prefix.
// CHECK: idr.func private @Prog.result() -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}con @Prog.Shape::@Rect(%{{[^,]+}}, %{{[^)]+}}) : (i64, i64) -> !idr.data<@Prog.Shape>
// CHECK: call @Prog.keep(%{{[^,)]+}}) : (i64) -> i64 loc("Prog.idr":
// CHECK: } loc("Prog.result"("Prog.idr":
// The other functions, in any order: a match on data has one case per
// constructor, its fields the region's arguments; one on an Int matches
// literals. keep and area are total, and keep has one parameter, v.
// countdown recurses on an Int: Idris does not prove that loop
// terminating, so its only fact is its instance. result has no loop of its
// own, so it is total though it calls countdown: whether a call of it may
// diverge is what it reaches (idr-effects); so is the root. A parameter is
// printed with its location, which holds no comma, hence the {{[^,]*}}
// after its type.
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func private @Prog.keep(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{[^,]*}}) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func private @Prog.area(%{{[^:]+}}: !idr.data<@Prog.Shape> {{[^,]*}}) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}match %{{[^ ]+}} : !idr.data<@Prog.Shape> -> (i64) {
// CHECK-DAG: case @Circle(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}) {
// CHECK-DAG: case @Rect(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}, %{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}) {
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func private @Prog.countdown(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{[^,]*}}) -> i64 attributes {instance = #idr.instance<"Prog.countdown"{{[^>]*}}>} {{[{]$}}
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}match_lit %{{[^ ]+}} : i64 -> (i64) {
// The root, the program on its world, is the only public function; its
// symbol is no bare identifier, so it prints quoted.
// CHECK: idr.func @"$idris-mlir.root"(%{{[^:]+}}: !idr.world {{.*}}) -> !idr.data<@{{"?}}PrimIO.IORes{{.*}}> attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
